   831		 * Now that the inodes are locked, we need to start writeback ourselves
   832		 * and can not rely on the writeback from the VFS's generic helper
   833		 * generic_remap_file_range_prep() because:
   834		 *
   835		 * 1) For compression we must call filemap_fdatawrite_range() range
   836		 *    twice (btrfs_fdatawrite_range() does it for us), and the generic
   837		 *    helper only calls it once;
   838		 *
   839		 * 2) filemap_fdatawrite_range(), called by the generic helper only
   840		 *    waits for the writeback to complete, i.e. for IO to be done, and
   841		 *    not for the ordered extents to complete. We need to wait for them
   842		 *    to complete so that new file extent items are in the fs tree.
   843		 */
   844		if (*len == 0 && !(remap_flags & REMAP_FILE_DEDUP))
